WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.915
Before changing a file, trace its impact. Here, five other files
depend on it.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:14.919
Start with a local scan. The deterministic scanner builds reusable
evidence from your source, without calling a language model.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:25.244
Locate a function to see its file, line range, and actual source. Then
inspect who has contributed to it.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:35.220
Follow the import graph beyond immediate neighbours. These paths show
how a change can reach the command line and the dashboard.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:46.804
Find related tests before you change the code. These eight candidates
guide investigation; they do not prove test coverage.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:57.207
Connect your coding agent through M C P. Targeted tool calls return
repository evidence, including source code and its location.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:04.823
In GitHub, a generated graph helps you trace the changed file to its
dependents.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:12.057
Read the findings alongside the code. Here, a review flags changed
count parsing.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:16.100
[Music and transition sounds]

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:26.221
Hosted features extend the evidence into architecture pages, symbol
documentation, and endpoint monitoring linked to source. Availability
depends on your plan.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:33.673
Start with your own repository. Install the free local scanner, and
follow the evidence from scan to review.
